      'Francisco L\u00f3pez works the opposite pole: conventional microphones, unconventional density. La Selva (1998) layers Costa Rican rainforest takes until individual sources dissolve into rain mass. The composition is in the layering — how many takes, at what levels, with what patience. Where Watson isolates and Winderen dives, L\u00f3pez accumulates. Three phonographers, three mix philosophies, one shared premise: the recording is the piece, not its document.',
      'For listeners building a practice: start with one microphone and learn it the way instrumentalists learn one instrument. A cheap contact mic on household objects teaches more about vibration than any textbook. Record the same source with air and contact mics and compare — the difference is orchestration. Watson\u2019s career, from Cabaret Voltaire\u2019s attic to Touch\u2019s field catalogue, demonstrates the continuity: close listening transfers across every transducer. The microphone changes. The attention does not.',
